                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Screw this game.\n\nI tried this game a long time ago...almost 10 years ago, and found it poor. Since then it has limped out of early access.\nIgnoring the lack of customisation options a second, basically everything about this game is very basic. The ‘tutorial’, to charitably call it that, is a slideshow presentation that features an outdated UI with text written pointing at stuff. But it was the developer’s first game, so I’m not too bothered by that.\nWhat I am bothered by is the insanely poor control you have over your character. This is an isometric crafty, base-buildy, survive the nighty kinda game. You move about with WASD or the mouse and use the mouse to try and break terrain, collect resources, and fight.\nI say try.\nThe thing your character chooses to break seems only tangentially connected to where your mouse is. Multiple times I broke things hidden INSIDE terrain, and frequently broke terrain above my character when my mouse was far to the right. Precision is a thing that happens in other games. If you misplace one wall, you’re gonna have to smash down five walls to try again.\nAs for the movement... I honestly didn’t know simple WASD movement controls could be this messed up. Yeah, stuff like GTA 5 has a single tap making you take several steps, but in this the game seemed almost to refuse to believe when I pressed more than one direction at a time; trying to move diagonally down and right, it would either go mostly down and a tiny bit right, or mostly right and a tiny bit down.\nAnd doorways... Oh hell. Trying to fit through a single-wide doorway was incredibly infuriating. I spent like a minute trying to walk into my own base. And automatic pathfinding isn’t any better. When I tried using the mouse to move, the character ran around the mountain trying to find the door directly in front of him.\n\nThrow in that the inventory, hotbar, and UI are very slow and clunky, and when crafting you have no idea what materials you have until they’re all gone and...yeah.\nI don’t want to bash this game too much, as it was clearly made by a first-time developer who didn’t really know what they were doing. But damn, this game is still for sale, claiming to be finished.\n\nThe final straw was when I was trying to move and accidentally clicked outside of the window. When I clicked back in, my character wouldn’t stop walking up. I literally had to save and quit to try and fix it...except the save didn’t load back in. It was just stuck forever on GENERATING WORLD.\nSo I shall repeat.\n\nScrew this game.",
